# Universal-variable export allowlist.
# Each line is a fish-style glob matched against universal variable names.
# Patterns are typically added by answering [t]rack in a wrangle session;
# manual edits work too.
#
# Comments (#) and blank lines ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT context — see https://github.com/fish-shell/fish-shell/issues/7379
#   * Fish universals are controversial and may be deprecated upstream.
#     Treat this file as a "necessary evil" for plugins (e.g. tide, sponge)
#     that use universals as their SOLE config persistence mechanism.
#   * Don't add patterns for fish native settings (theme colors, key
#     bindings) — those should be persisted via config.fish or function
#     files in home/.
#   * Don't add patterns for plugin INTERNAL state (typically `_<plugin>_*`
#     prefixed) — those are per-process caches, useless cross-machine.
